// Negative fixture for apply_models.py --validate-map --check-tiers (Phase 6;
// re-based and decontaminated in P10B). 'dick' is upstream sonnet (role
// 'reviewers'); this map silently retiers dick up to 'deep-reviewers' (opus
// tier) — an undisclosed upgrade. --check-tiers must reject it against
// tests/fixtures/upstream-tiers.tsv (exact tier match for every agent except
// sebastian, exempt by name — r5). Otherwise a full, structurally-valid
// 22-agent map: dick's old role 'reviewers' still has eight other agents and
// 'deep-reviewers' gains dick, so no role is orphaned and no file is uncovered
// — the ONLY failure is the tier upgrade.
//
// Decontamination note (P10B): the pre-P10B form moved 'codebase-locator'
// fast-scan -> builders, which structurally orphaned 'fast-scan' (codebase-
// locator is the sole haiku-upstream agent, so it must stay on fast-scan or
// something else must fill it — and any other agent there is itself a
// downgrade). That produced a SECOND, contaminating orphan-role FAIL once P7
// folded orphan detection into the shared validator — a reject-for-the-wrong-
// reason defect (P8). Retiering a multi-agent-role member instead yields
// exactly one FAIL.
